{
  "name": "flounder",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/fish/flounder.py): a flounder (the European plaice), 40 cm -- a FLAT OVAL LYING ON ITS SIDE, a thin disc in the ground plane; BOTH EYES ON THE TOP SIDE, close together on raised turrets, a row of bony KNOBS behind them, a small twisted mouth; the DORSAL and ANAL fins a long FRINGE round nearly the whole edge (one membrane sheet, mirrored to the other edge), a little pectoral flap on top, a short stalk and a rounded fan of a tail; brown above with bright ORANGE SPOTS, a pale blind side below. A SWIMMER near the bottom whose spine waves UP AND DOWN (about z), a flatfish's beat (the fish's plumbing).",
